\textbf{Baselines:} 
%To demonstrate the strength of our approach, 
We compare our framework against different types of SOTA planners, two behavior cloning-based planners (M$\pi$Nets~\cite{fishman2023motion}, MPNets~\cite{8793889_qureshi}) and two stochastic optimization-based planners (G. Fabrics~\cite{xie2021geometric}, STORM~\cite{bhardwaj2022storm}), one optimization-based planner with quintic-spline initialization (CHOMP~\cite{5152817_ratliff}), and a set of sampling-based planners through OMPL~\cite{6377468_sucan} on \textit{global}, \textit{hybrid}, and \textit{both} test sets. 

