\textbf{Metrics:} We define success rate (SR $\%$) as the percentage of problems that are successfully solved by the given planner. We say that a problem is successfully solved if the planner can generate a trajectory that avoids all collisions in order to reach the goal. 
M$\pi$Nets doesn't release the full global data, therefore the metrics are taken from the paper directly. 

