This evaluation aims to determine if the combination of synthetic and real data provides a substantial performance improvement.

\label{sec:results}

This section presents the results of our experiments, evaluating the performance of pain recognition models trained on different datasets: real, synthetic, and a combination of both. Subsequently, we provide an analysis of design decisions regarding the generation of synthetic data. The evaluation metrics used are Area Under the Receiver Operating Characteristic Curve (AUROC), F1-Score, and Accuracy. These metrics provide a comprehensive overview of the models' capabilities in handling the BioVid Heat Pain dataset, as detailed in Table \ref{tab:results}.

